======================================================================================================================
f22 -- THE CLUSTER THRESHOLD HUNT: is the scale where the framework stops working a Lambda scale?
======================================================================================================================

0.  THE SCALES THE FRAMEWORK OWNS (every 'Lambda scale' below is built from these and nothing else)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  rho_crit = 8.5331e-27 kg/m^3, Omega_Lambda = 0.6866, rho_Lambda = 5.8588e-27 kg/m^3, H_Lambda = 1.8099e-18 s^-1
  a_0 = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_Lambda) = 9.3732e-11 m/s^2  (canonical footing carried as 9.360e-11, alt 1.130e-10)
  Z = c H_Lambda / a_0 = 5.789   (sqrt(32 pi/3) = 5.789)
  Lambda LENGTHS: c/H_Lambda = 5368 Mpc, c^2/a_0 = 31118 Mpc, 1/sqrt(Lambda) = 3099 Mpc
  Lambda MASSES : de Sitter horizon mass 5.61e+22 Msun; r_M = r_S mass c^4/(4 G a_0) = 1.63e+23 Msun
  the dimensionless POTENTIALS available without a mass: a_0/(c H_Lambda) = 1/Z = 0.173 and its powers
  [PASS] 0a the framework's own a_0 is reproduced from rho_Lambda to the precision of the footing   (9.3732e-11 vs 9.360e-11)
  [PASS] 0b the kernel used here is the ledger's kernel (hunt_lib.nu_s), so B values are in the ledger's currency   (nu(0.5) = 1.972654 both ways)

